Project Demonstration Phase 
The Project Demonstration Phase is the stage where the completed project or prototype is presented to others to show how it works and explain its features.
Main steps:
Prepare the project – Make sure the project is complete and working.
Introduce the project – Explain the problem and purpose.
Demonstrate features – Show how the project works step by step.
Explain the results – Present the outcomes and benefits.
Answer questions – Respond to doubts and feedback.
Collect feedback – Use suggestions to improve the project.
